{"id": "EUVD-2026-102957", "enisaUuid": "904439dc-a005-3d3b-918e-3e6adb040c30", "description": "Steedos Platform through 3.0.15-beta.51 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows authenticated users to read other tenants' report definitions by querying the reports object. Because objectql's callAdapter skips space filtering for enable_space_global objects on find/findOne, attackers can call GET /api/v1/reports to disclose report names, descriptions, and object and field API names.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T21:18:06", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/steedos-platform-reports-cross-tenant-idor", "https://github.com/steedos/steedos-platform/blob/v3.0.15-beta.51/packages/objectql/src/types/object.ts#L2899-L2913", "https://github.com/steedos/steedos-platform/blob/v3.0.15-beta.51/services/service-core-objects/main/default/objects/reports.object.yml#L4", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/steedos-platform-through-3.0.15-beta.51-cross-tenant-information-disclosure-via-reports-api"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111666", "GHSA-388m-pwcw-qwh5"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7a422010-aec0-3d4e-b7e3-0f6782a7f7af", "product": {"name": "steedos-platform", "vendor": {"name": "steedos"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.0.15-beta.51"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "21ee7018-d8f0-3260-a7bc-c533dda906fc", "vendor": {"name": "steedos"}}], "isExploited": false}